alexxx wrote:
>
> As my magician is able to reach lower and lower depths,
> the problem of what to keep and what to discard due to weight becomes
> more and more present.
> I was wondering: there is some way in the game to store away some items
> that you don't continuously want to keep with you? E.g. in a bag on
> some initial level or something... or else the game randomly zaps those
> items away???

The good news: no; dropped items and items left on some other level
usually don't vanish (exceptions are most corpses that spoil after
some time and if you care to bury some organic material).  But there
are creatures that may eat stuff lying around; some eat metal, others
eat also objects of other materials. And there are monsters that may
destroy items if they are in line-of-fire between your and the
monsters position (cold breathing creatures may destroy potions, fire
breathing ones destroy scrolls and books, and the disintegration
blast... - well, I'll leave that to your imagination).

Items are best dropped close to the stairs where you leave the level;
that way you can make sure that no monster is close that might take or
destroy your loot. (Monsters don't move on the levels once you left
the respective levels.)

Yet better to put your objects in chests or boxes; there are quite
some available in the dungeons. There's no need to lock them because
monsters won't open containers, but there's still the possibility that
some monster might find that box quite tasty.

Another degree of safety is to engrave Elbereth on the square with the
box. A cursed object on top of the box will prevent your stronger pets
from removing the box from that place.

Finally the small branches, like Sokoban, are preferred levels where
to build your primary stashes.

